'''''Poe Dameron'' 9''' is the ninth issue of the [[Marvel Comics|Marvel]] [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] series ''[[Star Wars: Poe Dameron]]''. Written by [[Charles Soule]], with art by [[Phil Noto]], it was published on [[December 14]], [[2016]].

==Publisher's summary==
''*''Poe Dameron'' is on a secret mission from General Organa herself&hellip;''''
''*''&hellip;to escort none other than C-3PO on a dangerous mission to the planet Kaddak!''''
''*''Also: a sneak peek into Terex's past&hellip;''''

==Opening crawl==
{{OpeningCrawl
|name=Book III, Part II<br />THE GATHERING STORM
|text=It is a time of uncertainty in the galaxy. Standing
against the oppression of the First Order is General
Organa's Resistance, including Poe Dameron and his
team of ace pilots &mdash; Black Squadron.

Black Squadron has undertaken a mission to find the
explorer Lor San Tekka, and a new enemy has emerged:
Terex, an officer of the First Order Security
Bureau. Though Poe's crew of pilots managed to
survive multiple encounters, Terex has vowed to
destroy them.

Meanwhile, the droid C-3PO has approached Poe with an
urgent undertaking &mdash; to retrieve information and
rescue a droid operative on the planet Kaddak. But
what they don't know is that Terex is on Kaddak,
too....}}

==Plot summary==
On the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] world of [[Kaddak]], [[Poe Dameron]] along with the technician [[Oddy Muva]], the [[protocol droid]] [[C-3PO]], and the [[astromech droid]] [[R2-D2]] began searching for the [[Resistance spy droid network|droid spy]]. Shortly after landing, the Resistance agents see a person being thrown to his death, emphasizing Kaddak's reputation as as seedy, crime have.

As Terex walks through the streets of [[Sliver|The Sliver]] on [[Level 72]], a [[Zabrak]] child attempted to steal from him. Terex caught the child, but the mother quickly apologized. Terex contemplates shooting the child but instead shows mercy and gives him a [[credit chip]]. At a bar, the customers are shocked at Terex's return. He walks to his favorite table, where decades earlier [[Corlac]] brought him to meet with [[Wenda]] and [[Bett]].

Corlac claims Wenda and Bett would help them bring back the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]], and Terex revealed that he used to work at base defense at the [[Rothana Imperial Shipyards|shipyard]] on [[Rothana]] before he was reassigned to [[Jakku]]. They formulated a plan to go to [[Rothana]], take the remaining [[Starship|ships]], and quietly send messages to the remaining Imperials to build a fleet and rebuild the Empire. Wenda and Bett would help them in return for unusable parts for their salvage and repair operation.

Back in the present day, [[C-3PO]] waited for an operative that had information about the droid spy. He mentioned [[Han Solo]], attracting the attention of [[Kanjiklub]] nearby. The operative, a [[MSE-6 series repair droid|mouse droid]], arrived, and downloaded the information into [[BB-8]]. Meanwhile, Kanjiklub met with the [[Guavian Death Gang]], and the rival organizations agreed to work together due to their mutual hatred of Solo. BB-8 revealed that the droid spy is being held by the [[Ranc Gang|Rancs]], an especially dangerous organization.

In the bar, Terex met with the Rancs and their leader, [[Wisper]]. In the past, Terex gained access to the repair bay on Rothana, and Wisper led her team in.

In the present day, Wisper welcomed Terex back, but drew her [[blaster]] when he revealed he wanted to take back control of the Rancs. He drew a blade, forcing her to drop the blaster. She claimed that she was the leader after he gave her control and joined the [[First Order]], but Terex pointed out that none of the Rancs had killed him. Wisper pleaded with them to follow her, but [[Zumgi]] shot her and welcomed Terex.

C-3PO led the way to the Ranc base, while Dameron warned [[Oddy Muva|Muva]] to stay alert. C-3PO spoke with a man about the droid, but the man drew a blaster and stunned Dameron.

